  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q63-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "63",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3x^2-2x+5}{(x-6)(x+2)}$, $x\\ne6,-2$.\n\nUse a common denominator and subtract each entire numerator.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2+1}{(x-6)(x+2)}-\\frac{x+2}{(x-6)(x+2)}-\\frac{x-6}{(x-6)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2+1-(x+2)-(x-6)}{(x-6)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3x^2+1}{x^2-4x-12}-\\frac1{x-6}-\\frac1{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2-2x+5}{(x-6)(x+2)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne6,-2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
